@packages/compiler/src/proposal-workspace.sigil import { SigilProposalWorkspace }

component SigilCompilationSessionStore {
  goal {
    Persist and serialize local compilation sessions across independent CLI
    processes without a daemon or selected-workspace mutation.

    Keep session discovery, caller isolation, record durability, and operation
    locking separate from proposal materialization and compilation evaluation.
  }

  interface {
    CompilationSessionStorage {
      create(sessionIdentity, sessionRecord) validates a version-1 SessionRecord,
      atomically creates an owner-private session beneath the operating-system
      temporary directory, and returns its verified record and exclusive SessionLease
      or rejects with a stable invalid-session, ownership, state, or host-failure
      code

      open(sessionIdentity) validates the stored identity, ownership marker, and
      version-1 SessionRecord and returns its verified record and exclusive
      SessionLease, including when lifecycle state is expired, or rejects with a
      stable invalid-session, ownership, busy, state, or host-failure code

      commit(SessionLease, sessionRecord) validates the lease, storage envelope,
      identity, ownership, version, and structural state, atomically replaces the
      durable record, and retains the lease on success or failure; invalid or
      released lease, envelope, version, identity, or state mismatch rejects with
      COMPILER_WORKSPACE_STATE, unverifiable ownership rejects with
      COMPILER_WORKSPACE_OWNERSHIP_UNVERIFIED, and write, sync, or atomic replacement
      failure rejects with COMPILER_WORKSPACE_HOST_FAILURE

      remove(SessionLease) removes only the verified session record and container
      after proposal-workspace cleanup and releases the lease on success; rejection
      preserves recovery evidence and retains the lease; invalid or released lease,
      envelope, version, identity, or state mismatch rejects with
      COMPILER_WORKSPACE_STATE, unverifiable ownership rejects with
      COMPILER_WORKSPACE_OWNERSHIP_UNVERIFIED, and verified removal failure rejects
      with COMPILER_WORKSPACE_HOST_FAILURE
    }

    SessionRecord {
      version 1 contains session identity, selected workspace identity, target,
      profile, focus, capability contract, lifecycle state, expiry, base epoch,
      generation identity, base and proposal fingerprints, opaque
      ProposalWorkspacePersistedState, and latest completed report identity

      contains no proposed source contents, credentials, temporary path, or hidden
      evaluator reasoning
    }

    SessionLease {
      represents one nonblocking exclusive operating-system file lock and the
      verified session record for one CLI operation

      release unlocks and closes its file handle idempotently
    }
  }
}

expand SigilCompilationSessionStore {
  logic {
    CompilationSessionStorage {
      Resolve one private compiler-session parent through the host operating-system
      temporary-directory facility and derive the child name from the validated
      canonical session UUID.

      Use one persistent lock file per session. Acquire a nonblocking exclusive
      Deno.FsFile lock before reading or changing session state and return
      COMPILER_SESSION_BUSY when another process owns the lock.

      Return the verified record with the lease and leave proposal-workspace restore,
      access release, and close ordering to SigilCompilationSession. Commit state
      through write, sync, and atomic replacement while retaining the lease.

      Let operating-system file locks release automatically when a process exits.
      Never add a daemon, process registry, stale-lock timer, or bearer credential.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    CompilationSessionStorage {
      The session parent, each session directory, lock file, record, marker, and
      materialized proposal workspace are accessible only to the creating operating-
      system user whenever the host can enforce owner-private storage.

      A UUID version 4 session identity locates a record but never authorizes access.
      Access additionally requires the creating operating-system user's filesystem
      authority plus exact record and ownership-marker validation.

      Reject symbolic links, unexpected file kinds, invalid outer record schemas,
      identity mismatch, and ownership mismatch before returning a record or
      performing storage cleanup. Leave ProposalWorkspacePersistedState compatibility
      and record-to-materialization consistency to SigilProposalWorkspace.

      Support exactly SessionRecord version 1. Reject an unsupported version or
      malformed record with COMPILER_WORKSPACE_STATE, preserve its directory for
      recovery, and perform no migration.

      A rejected commit leaves the preceding valid record durable and retains the
      SessionLease for explicit cleanup or release. No opener observes a partial
      replacement.

      Commit and remove verify storage ownership before classifying other failures.
      Unverifiable ownership takes precedence as
      COMPILER_WORKSPACE_OWNERSHIP_UNVERIFIED. Invalid or released lease, storage-
      envelope, schema, version, identity, or structural-state mismatch rejects with
      COMPILER_WORKSPACE_STATE. Write, sync, atomic replacement, or verified removal
      failure rejects with COMPILER_WORKSPACE_HOST_FAILURE. Every rejection retains
      the lease and preserves recovery evidence.

      Proposed Sigil contents remain only in the private materialized proposal
      workspace. SessionRecord never duplicates them.

      Failure to enforce the owner-private boundary or durable atomic update rejects
      with COMPILER_WORKSPACE_HOST_FAILURE rather than broadening access.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    LocalSessionPersistence {
      Decision: Persist compilation sessions in owner-private operating-system
      temporary storage and coordinate independent CLI processes with advisory file
      locks instead of a daemon.

      Scope: Governs local session discovery, serialization, durability, and
      operation exclusion; excludes proposal contents and compilation semantics.

      Assumptions: The host exposes an owner-private temporary directory and releases
      advisory locks when the holding process exits.

      Trade-offs: Session continuity depends on local temporary storage and is not
      portable between users or hosts.

      Discarded alternatives: A background daemon, repository-local session state,
      and UUID bearer authorization were rejected as unnecessary infrastructure,
      workspace mutation, or an unsafe trust boundary.

      Consequences: Separate CLI invocations can safely resume one local session
      without retaining a process or treating the session identifier as a secret.
    }

    AtomicSessionRecordCommit {
      Decision: Validate and atomically replace one versioned session record while an
      explicit operation lease remains held.

      Scope: Governs record compatibility, commit visibility, and lease disposition;
      excludes proposal-workspace lifecycle and session settlement.

      Trade-offs: Version mismatch fails closed and requires recovery or cleanup
      rather than implicit migration.

      Design issues addressed: Independent processes must never observe partial state
      or infer whether a failed commit released serialization.

      Consequences: A caller can coordinate cleanup after failure while later openers
      observe either the preceding valid record or the complete replacement.
    }
  }

  cases {
    CompilationSessionStorage {
      A second CLI process opening a currently locked session receives
      COMPILER_SESSION_BUSY without waiting or changing state.

      Process exit releases its advisory lock and permits a later command to open the
      unchanged durable record.

      Interruption before atomic replacement leaves the preceding valid record
      observable. Successful replacement exposes the complete new record, and no
      opener can observe a partial record.

      Commit rejection preserves the preceding record and retains the lease until the
      caller releases it or verified removal succeeds.

      Commit or remove with unverifiable ownership rejects with
      COMPILER_WORKSPACE_OWNERSHIP_UNVERIFIED even when another state defect is also
      present and preserves recovery evidence.

      Commit or remove with an invalid or released lease, malformed envelope,
      unsupported version, identity mismatch, or structural-state mismatch rejects
      with COMPILER_WORKSPACE_STATE and retains the lease when one remains held.

      Commit write, sync, or atomic-replacement failure and verified removal failure
      reject with COMPILER_WORKSPACE_HOST_FAILURE, retain the lease, and preserve
      recovery evidence.

      Opening an expired record returns its record and lease so close may perform
      expiry cleanup; evaluate and refresh enforce expiry after open.

      An unsupported record version rejects with COMPILER_WORKSPACE_STATE without
      migration, proposal inspection, or automatic removal.

      Another operating-system user, a symbolic-link substitution, or a mismatched
      marker cannot open or delete the session.

      A missing or malformed record rejects without inspecting or removing proposal
      contents.
    }
  }
}
